{
  "dom_id": "question-142571",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14188481/assets/4c9b1e09734e74c098fd5e91eb3c72079157c3a69b1bb1d039bb46e823e5b7b6.png)\n\nConsider a sample of size $n=25$ from a normal population. Given that the sample mean is $35.5,$ and the sample standard deviation is $3,$ find a $95%$ confidence interval for the population mean $\\mu $ of the distribution.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>2.064)=0.025,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $24$ degrees of freedom,  as shown in the diagram above.*",
